{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pulls/54","id":4594768665,"node_id":"PR_kwDORfqZes8AAAABEd6bGQ","html_url":"https://github.com/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pull/54","diff_url":"https://github.com/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pull/54.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pull/54.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/issues/54","number":54,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Keep Inspector outputs current and package standalone startup","user":{"login":"michaeljgrimm","id":12368053,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzY4MDUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12368053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm","html_url":"https://github.com/michaeljgrimm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Inspector share URLs and toolbar actions could read delayed preview state after source edits or imports. Automatic publication now verifies the current source before and after encoding. Explicit Copy, JSON, Share, PPTX/PDF and Author/Deckchat actions commit pending public canvas drafts and use one guarded source snapshot for the payload and filename. Rejected drafts remain visible to the action after pointer-blur recovery; newer source, navigation and action intent suppress stale results.\n\nProduction startup packages Next standalone output with its assets, fonts and traced schema inputs. Generated dependency links, including `.next/node_modules` aliases, are normalized to relative internal targets with explicit file/directory types and verified before launch. Font preparation and converter warmup now run concurrently; preview still waits for both, preserving offline export readiness. Failed preparation disposes any eventually successful font registry. The complete font inventory, measurement policy and existing readiness gates remain unchanged.\n\nValidation of the current font orchestration change: independent source review, 12 focused ownership/failure controls, the full 704-test unit suite, 13 standalone controls, a fresh production build and all 39 unchanged local browser cases pass on Node 24 with zero browser retries. The offline Author/Inspector export/reimport flows pass; all 33 font files and the complete manifest match the prior build exactly. Root reviewed all four changed screenshot pairs and two targeted recovery/font-notes frames. Fresh Linux/Windows CI and release acceptance remain required for `a4eb88ab7aa585c9efb91de4c190c1f1c0c7d0eb`. [Preserved failure, source reviews and fresh local evidence](https://github.com/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/blob/a4eb88ab7aa585c9efb91de4c190c1f1c0c7d0eb/docs/evidence/font-preparation-concurrency-20260921/README.md).\n\nEarlier failures remain evidence: the original Windows security readiness timeout, archived-source typecheck failure, standalone startup EPERM, and head `4338e57` Windows result of 38/39 in [CI35649707689](https://github.com/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/actions/runs/35649707689). The latter stopped before editing/recovery with the correct source and “Loading slide fonts…”. Its trace records delayed font requests without a completed response for eleven fonts before teardown; it does not establish permanent failure or isolate the dominant bottleneck. The concurrency change removes an unnecessary sequence while retaining the both-ready requirement; fresh Windows acceptance remains required.\n\nPDF/Deckchat checks use local mocks. URL handoffs preserve semantics; exact action bytes refer to the accepted buffer after ingress normalization. Already-started side effects cannot be cancelled retroactively. The protected Vercel preview boundary, canonical production acceptance, native Office/font compatibility, and the separate suggestion-details/preset candidates remain distinct. Issue88 remains OPEN. No package publication or native compatibility completion is part of this PR.\n","created_at":"2026-09-21T18:24:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-21T21:02:40Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8b65b701fb588bba18108a3d59e2c480efd7a657","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pulls/54/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pulls/54/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/issues/54/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/statuses/a4eb88ab7aa585c9efb91de4c190c1f1c0c7d0eb","head":{"label":"Data-Advantage:codex/inspector-share-guard-20260921","ref":"codex/inspector-share-guard-20260921","sha":"a4eb88ab7aa585c9efb91de4c190c1f1c0c7d0eb","user":{"login":"Data-Advantage","id":104524841,"node_id":"O_kgDOBjrsKQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104524841?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Data-Advantage","html_url":"https://github.com/Data-Advantage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Data-Advantage/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Data-Advantage/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Da